{% extends 'base.twig' %}{% block content %}<section class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">THE WORK, AS IT HAPPENS</p><h1>Built in the open.<br><span class="serif">One release at a time.</span></h1><p>What changed, what works, and what’s coming next.<br>No mystery versions. Just a clear record of progress.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/feed.xml">Subscribe with Atom ↗</a></section><section class="container updates-layout"><aside><a class="tag" href="#development-preview">Development preview</a><p class="muted small">Stable releases will appear here<br>after compatibility and release checks.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/roadmap">Explore the roadmap →</a></aside><article class="release-entry" id="development-preview"><div class="release-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-29">October 29, 2026</time><span class="tag">0.1.0-dev</span></div><h2>A small beginning.<br>A working foundation.</h2><p>The first Elang development snapshot brings the application kernel, modular services, and a documentation website running on Elang itself.</p><h3>Available in this preview</h3><ul><li>Named routes, parameter requirements, groups, and middleware.</li><li>A PSR-11 service container with constructor injection.</li><li>Twig views and Symfony constraint-based validation.</li><li>Doctrine DBAL, migrations, and a standalone application generator.</li><li>Sessions, CSRF middleware, password hashing, encryption, and rate limiting.</li><li>Cache, logging, events, mail transport, and console commands.</li><li>Versioned English documentation, lessons, examples, and Markdown exports.</li></ul><h3>Before a stable release</h3><p>We need broader application testing, a documented compatibility policy, independent security review, and feedback on the public APIs. An ORM, full authentication, queues, and a scheduler are not included yet.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/docs/v0.1/installation">Explore the preview →</a></article></section>{% endblock %}
